WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.884
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.154 --> 00:10.491
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:49.738
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:49.864 --> 00:51.282
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.658 --> 00:53.492
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.617 --> 00:54.451
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.577 --> 00:55.411
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.536 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:56.495 --> 00:59.290
[quirky instrumental music playing]

10
01:01.625 --> 01:03.085
What an attention seeker.

11
01:03.586 --> 01:04.920
You'd think she's done directing.

12
01:05.504 --> 01:08.632
That makes no sense. If Mi-do quits directing,

13
01:08.757 --> 01:10.968
I swear I'll send her my entire life savings.

14
01:11.093 --> 01:14.054
Muyeong Bank, 073-0214.

15
01:14.889 --> 01:17.057
I bet it's minuscule, but it's better than nothing.

16
01:17.182 --> 01:18.517
[hesitates] Minuscule?

17
01:18.642 --> 01:19.602
Hey!

18
01:22.438 --> 01:23.606
Oh, Mom.

19
01:30.905 --> 01:32.573
[music concludes]

20
01:32.698 --> 01:34.783
[Suk-hee] The rice store owner's youngest son

21
01:34.909 --> 01:37.411
passed the civil service exam a few days ago,

22
01:37.536 --> 01:41.248
and the eldest daughter of the piano academy owner

23
01:41.373 --> 01:42.541
just got into college.

24
01:42.666 --> 01:43.667
It was her fourth try.

25
01:43.792 --> 01:45.836
You know, I'm really done with directing.

26
01:51.216 --> 01:53.344
Whatever Yeong-do says, don't stress.

27
01:54.094 --> 01:57.306
Don't forget, your fortune says you're a late bloomer.

28
01:57.431 --> 01:59.058
-[sighs] -[Suk-hee] Your birth chart…

29
01:59.892 --> 02:02.353
says all good things take time for you.

30
02:02.478 --> 02:04.146
I'm serious about quitting.

31
02:05.856 --> 02:09.360
This month, I'll get the merchant savings club payout.

32
02:10.152 --> 02:12.571
I can lend you that money, so don't worry about that.

33
02:12.696 --> 02:13.656
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

34
02:13.781 --> 02:17.201
[Suk-hee] Focus on writing your script. It'll take you about two years, okay?

35
02:17.326 --> 02:19.703
Don't worry. I'll lend it to you without any interest.

36
02:25.918 --> 02:27.002
Hey. Hey, hey, hey. Wait.

37
02:27.252 --> 02:28.295
THE 13TH SEASON

38
02:28.462 --> 02:29.922
-[Suk-hee] Are you crazy? -[sighs]

39
02:30.172 --> 02:31.590
Oh, my God. Are you crazy?

40
02:31.715 --> 02:33.509
Didn't you hear what I just said?

41
02:34.093 --> 02:36.637
I said I'm quitting directing and you don't really care!

42
02:37.513 --> 02:39.181
Why won't anyone believe me?

43
02:39.682 --> 02:42.643
Nobody listens to a word I say! [sobs]

44
02:45.646 --> 02:49.066
Ma, I said it because I'm truly struggling.

45
02:49.525 --> 02:50.985
I really feel bad for you.

46
02:51.527 --> 02:54.530
I know I'm letting you down and even then it was just too hard.

47
02:54.655 --> 02:57.157
I just gathered the courage to tell you the truth.

48
02:57.950 --> 03:02.246
Are you saying you're actually gonna quit directing?

49
03:02.705 --> 03:03.664
Yeah.

50
03:03.789 --> 03:05.124
That's exactly what I said.

51
03:05.582 --> 03:07.167
I won't direct anything again!

52
03:07.292 --> 03:08.669
You sacrificed your youth!

53
03:09.712 --> 03:12.131
How can you just throw it away because it's hard?

54
03:12.715 --> 03:14.925
You have to fight even harder for it!

55
03:15.426 --> 03:17.469
Just bite down and get through it!

56
03:19.096 --> 03:22.057
Listen, if you give up now, you'll be a failure and regret it.

57
03:22.516 --> 03:23.600
You hear me?

58
03:23.726 --> 03:25.019
[sobs] Ma…

59
03:25.144 --> 03:29.398
[somber piano music playing]

60
03:29.523 --> 03:30.482
A failure?

61
03:30.607 --> 03:32.568
Exactly. A failure.

62
03:33.944 --> 03:35.904
I'm sorry. [breathes shakily]

63
03:36.030 --> 03:37.531
I'm a complete failure.

64
03:38.824 --> 03:40.409
What? What are you…

65
03:40.534 --> 03:42.828
What are you doing? You little… That's enough!

66
03:42.953 --> 03:45.039
-How dare you say that? -[Namgung] No, stop! Please don't!

67
03:45.164 --> 03:46.206
That hurts.

68
03:48.333 --> 03:51.128
-Calm down. -[gasps]

69
03:51.378 --> 03:52.421
Easy.

70
03:53.130 --> 03:54.089
Just put that down.

71
03:57.051 --> 04:01.013
[sobbing]

72
04:01.138 --> 04:03.140
[arcade machine whirring, buttons clicking]

73
04:18.072 --> 04:19.073
Sorry…

74
04:19.740 --> 04:21.200
I didn't tell you sooner.

75
04:21.325 --> 04:22.659
Well, you couldn't.

76
04:23.660 --> 04:25.120
She must have threatened you.

77
04:27.122 --> 04:28.707
Giving you a really hard time.

78
04:30.584 --> 04:34.838
Even so, out of the four of you, Mi-do is the kindest.

79
04:34.963 --> 04:36.840
Yeong-do is the softest.

80
04:37.591 --> 04:39.343
Wan-do is the meanest.

81
04:40.636 --> 04:41.637
And as for you…

82
04:45.682 --> 04:47.226
I ain't gonna say it.

83
04:48.143 --> 04:49.353
You always hold your tongue,

84
04:49.978 --> 04:52.106
so I have the right to keep one secret too.

85
04:55.651 --> 04:57.528
Now go and comfort the kind one.

86
04:58.403 --> 05:00.489
Your support does more than anything I can do.

87
05:00.614 --> 05:03.534
[somber piano music continues]

88
05:15.712 --> 05:22.594
[footsteps approaching]

89
05:26.431 --> 05:27.766
[music concludes]

90
05:35.023 --> 05:36.942
She must have won 20 of them today.

91
05:39.111 --> 05:40.362
Thirty-two.

92
05:42.531 --> 05:43.490
[sighs]

93
05:48.704 --> 05:49.830
Hey, Mi-do.

94
05:50.873 --> 05:52.416
Are you really sure about this?

95
05:55.878 --> 05:57.588
Are you sure you won't regret it?

96
05:58.672 --> 06:00.465
I had an interview last week.

97
06:01.049 --> 06:02.509
And I had my first day today.

98
06:04.428 --> 06:06.096
It's decent. Good prospects, too.

99
06:09.558 --> 06:11.393
My life sunk to a new low point,

100
06:12.728 --> 06:14.104
and our relationship…

101
06:16.315 --> 06:18.233
crashed and burned to ashes.

102
06:23.363 --> 06:25.490
Honestly, I'm terrified about this.

103
06:28.035 --> 06:30.037
But I'm also not afraid.

104
06:34.124 --> 06:35.083
[sighs softly]

105
06:38.253 --> 06:39.713
Tell me, did you ask her?

106
06:42.341 --> 06:44.801
[tender piano music playing]

107
06:44.927 --> 06:46.553
[Namgung] Would you date me just for a month?

108
06:46.678 --> 06:48.305
[insects chirping]

109
06:51.934 --> 06:52.893
Yeah.

110
06:54.978 --> 06:55.938
I would.

111
06:58.774 --> 07:00.108
Let's give us a shot.

112
07:01.735 --> 07:02.694
Sure.

113
07:05.906 --> 07:06.865
[sighs softly]

114
07:11.245 --> 07:12.287
And you?

115
07:16.166 --> 07:17.542
[Mi-do] One month.

116
07:17.668 --> 07:19.419
Do you want to lose your mind with me?

117
07:20.254 --> 07:21.255
You up for the challenge?

118
07:26.760 --> 07:27.803
You know…

119
07:32.599 --> 07:34.768
if you date me, you won't go back.

120
07:38.063 --> 07:40.565
I'll do everything I can to win you over.

121
07:42.818 --> 07:44.111
[sighs]

122
07:52.953 --> 07:55.289
[inhales deeply] It's just one month.

123
07:58.125 --> 08:00.460
We're just breaking up for 30 days, and we--

124
08:00.585 --> 08:01.712
For that time…

125
08:04.256 --> 08:06.675
we'll do our best with our new partners.

126
08:07.384 --> 08:09.344
And starting this exact moment…

127
08:12.431 --> 08:14.850
we hit pause and are officially on a break.

128
08:20.230 --> 08:24.818
[music rises]

129
08:26.028 --> 08:27.070
[ring clatters]

130
08:47.632 --> 08:51.511
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

131
08:51.678 --> 08:56.224
DO YOU REMEMBER WHEN WE FELL IN LOVE?

132
08:56.350 --> 08:57.517
[music concludes]

133
08:57.642 --> 08:59.561
[soft music playing over speakers]

134
09:05.359 --> 09:08.028
[cutlery clinking, scraping]

135
09:09.738 --> 09:11.782
-Let me ask you something. -I'll say something first.

136
09:11.907 --> 09:12.991
[clears throat]

137
09:14.576 --> 09:15.660
You're right.

138
09:16.203 --> 09:17.454
I have feelings for you.

139
09:17.579 --> 09:19.748
Based on a completely objective self-analysis,

140
09:19.998 --> 09:22.626
you were the one I turned to during the sweet potato scandal.

141
09:23.794 --> 09:26.963
And I think I'm making the error of mistaking platonic feelings

142
09:27.089 --> 09:28.131
for romance.

143
09:28.256 --> 09:29.716
That's what's going on. Hmm.

144
09:30.425 --> 09:32.469
My goal for this month is to fix that error.

145
09:36.264 --> 09:37.432
I don't think it's that.

146
09:40.519 --> 09:43.397
You do like me a lot.

147
09:43.522 --> 09:44.606
[bright whimsical music playing]

148
09:44.731 --> 09:46.733
[Namgung] Like you said, you struggled with the scandal,

149
09:46.858 --> 09:48.693
and I was the only one who supported you.

150
09:48.819 --> 09:52.364
But the issue is, I ended up getting transferred because of you.

151
09:52.614 --> 09:54.783
That must have been the trigger for everything.

152
09:55.826 --> 09:58.787
When you feel that much guilt over someone in particular,

153
09:58.912 --> 10:01.248
that feeling gains momentum and lots of power.

154
10:01.790 --> 10:03.375
You feel sorry, so you care.

155
10:03.500 --> 10:05.168
You care, so you keep looking at them.

156
10:05.293 --> 10:07.921
And then you realize you can't keep that guy out of your head.

157
10:08.880 --> 10:09.840
Here's that guy.

158
10:11.550 --> 10:13.468
It's obvious I'm handsome, I have mature charm,

159
10:13.593 --> 10:14.928
I rock a suit, and have swagger.

160
10:15.053 --> 10:16.888
My intellect makes others feel secure.

161
10:17.013 --> 10:19.182
Plus, I'm great at my job. It's insane.

162
10:20.058 --> 10:21.726
Taking all this into account,

163
10:21.852 --> 10:25.063
it's understandable that you like your senior colleague.

164
10:25.188 --> 10:27.482
And that colleague is me, so I get it.

165
10:28.400 --> 10:30.193
[bright whimsical music continues]

166
10:31.736 --> 10:34.322
What are you saying? [chuckles awkwardly]

167
10:34.948 --> 10:36.700
-[music concludes] -Are you crazy?

168
10:36.825 --> 10:39.369
So I'm completely head over heels for you?

169
10:39.494 --> 10:41.288
Is that the nonsense you're trying to say?

170
10:41.413 --> 10:42.497
Not at all.

171
10:43.039 --> 10:44.166
It's just a cringe phase

172
10:44.291 --> 10:47.377
that you go through at your level with your senior.

173
10:48.086 --> 10:49.129
That's what I'm saying.

174
10:50.338 --> 10:51.798
And I'm sure in a month,

175
10:51.923 --> 10:54.301
I'll be a truly embarrassing memory for you.

176
10:55.302 --> 10:57.888
[munches]

177
10:59.264 --> 11:01.224
[inhales deeply, sighs]

178
11:01.766 --> 11:02.976
And the intimacy?

179
11:03.894 --> 11:06.188
[mischievous music rises, falls]

180
11:06.313 --> 11:08.440
How much touching is allowed?

181
11:08.565 --> 11:11.776
[mischievous music rises, falls]

182
11:12.444 --> 11:14.112
How much can you tolerate?

183
11:14.237 --> 11:16.531
-[chuckles] -[mischievous music continues]

184
11:16.656 --> 11:19.075
Why set limits, we're adults after all?

185
11:19.826 --> 11:22.204
Shouldn't everything be allowed?

186
11:22.329 --> 11:23.747
That so?

187
11:23.872 --> 11:26.917
[funky upbeat music playing]

188
11:27.042 --> 11:28.251
Shall we go?

189
11:48.563 --> 11:49.648
[hotel employee] Here's the key, sir.

190
11:50.690 --> 11:52.692
-[elevator bell chimes] -[automated voice] Going up.

191
11:54.778 --> 11:56.154
Careful, doors closing.

192
12:01.076 --> 12:04.996
-[cabinet door closes] -[music concludes]

193
12:09.668 --> 12:10.919
[sighs]

194
12:17.551 --> 12:19.010
Wanna take a shower?

195
12:21.179 --> 12:23.014
-Should I go first? -[gasps softly]

196
12:25.016 --> 12:26.101
Yeah, sure. Go ahead.

197
12:27.269 --> 12:28.478
-Okay. -Wait, no.

198
12:30.105 --> 12:31.398
I'll shower first.

199
12:38.405 --> 12:39.906
[breathes deeply]

200
12:43.743 --> 12:44.744
[chuckles awkwardly]

201
12:52.460 --> 12:53.545
[sighs]

202
12:55.005 --> 12:56.256
Hey,

203
12:57.674 --> 12:58.633
Park Su-a.

204
13:00.302 --> 13:02.012
I mean, Park Deok-sun.

205
13:02.637 --> 13:04.723
If a guy asks you to a hotel on the very first date,

206
13:04.848 --> 13:06.808
you smack him in the head and leave.

207
13:06.933 --> 13:08.560
Why follow me here blindly?

208
13:09.311 --> 13:12.606
I just waited to see how far you'd go, and you went to the end.

209
13:12.731 --> 13:14.399
-You've lost it. -[gasps softly]

210
13:14.941 --> 13:19.154
I think that just like your values, politics, and morals,

211
13:19.279 --> 13:21.906
knowing each other's sexual preferences is vital.

212
13:22.991 --> 13:24.034
You know?

213
13:25.076 --> 13:28.204
Physical intimacy is the fastest way to know each other. [chuckles nervously]

214
13:28.330 --> 13:32.459
Above all, in this country, we have sexual autonomy, right?

215
13:33.126 --> 13:34.085
Try it again.

216
13:36.504 --> 13:39.049
Two adults, both in agreement, coming to a hotel…

217
13:39.174 --> 13:40.634
[footsteps thud]

218
13:41.134 --> 13:42.260
Try it again.

219
13:43.928 --> 13:46.139
Is it a problem, legally or anything like that?

220
13:47.140 --> 13:48.516
Again.

221
13:48.642 --> 13:49.768
I'm being criticized about this

222
13:49.893 --> 13:51.227
-even when it's not-- -[footsteps thud]

223
13:51.353 --> 13:52.395
Again.

224
13:52.937 --> 13:56.232
I just think if we try it and it's not good,

225
13:56.358 --> 13:59.110
those feelings will erase fast and then just-- [groans]

226
14:00.612 --> 14:01.571
[sighs]

227
14:03.031 --> 14:06.368
[soft playful music playing]

228
14:12.082 --> 14:13.208
[sighs]

229
14:16.378 --> 14:17.712
[sighs]

230
14:19.506 --> 14:20.548
You're right.

231
14:21.132 --> 14:22.884
I like you more than you know, okay?

232
14:24.427 --> 14:29.724
And this is crazy, but that's why I agreed to that ridiculous one-month thing.

233
14:30.975 --> 14:32.769
You said you were curious, weren't you?

234
14:33.436 --> 14:34.562
Were you lying about that?

235
14:34.688 --> 14:36.356
I'm only curious.

236
14:37.524 --> 14:39.943
If your feelings get too deep, it won't work.

237
14:50.328 --> 14:53.665
[Mi-do panting]

238
14:53.790 --> 14:57.460
Ow. [panting]

239
14:58.712 --> 14:59.754
Wow.

240
14:59.879 --> 15:01.172
You don't last long at all.

241
15:01.297 --> 15:04.634
You have zero clients and are practically unemployed.

242
15:04.759 --> 15:07.429
At my new job, I work five days a week.

243
15:07.887 --> 15:10.014
Even so, I fully dressed up out of courtesy.

244
15:10.140 --> 15:12.559
I mean, why am I walking 5,000 steps on a first date?

245
15:12.809 --> 15:14.060
[soft playful music continues]

246
15:14.185 --> 15:15.353
Does this make sense to you?

247
15:17.856 --> 15:19.399
I bet your feet hurt.

248
15:19.899 --> 15:22.819
Jeez, how can you even say that? [sighs]

249
15:33.872 --> 15:34.956
Why not both?

250
15:35.081 --> 15:37.083
I don't like you enough to do that.

251
15:37.208 --> 15:38.293
[scoffs]

252
15:38.793 --> 15:39.753
[huffs]

253
15:42.922 --> 15:44.674
[grunts, exhales]

254
15:52.891 --> 15:54.184
Oh!

255
15:57.604 --> 15:58.813
[gasps]

256
15:59.939 --> 16:01.274
[chuckles softly]

257
16:03.943 --> 16:05.111
[hesitates] Wait!

258
16:06.321 --> 16:07.363
[exhales sharply]

259
16:07.489 --> 16:08.698
[music concludes]

260
16:12.577 --> 16:15.121
"I'm the illegitimate son from one of these homes."

261
16:15.246 --> 16:16.664
Don't you dare say that crap.

262
16:17.207 --> 16:18.208
Huh.

263
16:19.959 --> 16:22.962
So you failed as a director 'cause you lack imagination?

264
16:23.630 --> 16:26.966
You got dumped by your law firm and have no cases, so shut up now.

265
16:29.093 --> 16:31.095
[Tae-seung] They found me right here on this corner.

266
16:31.221 --> 16:33.848
My so-called mother watched too many drama series.

267
16:34.808 --> 16:37.477
She thought I'd grow up rich if she left me at a mansion.

268
16:41.606 --> 16:43.107
I'll show you where it all started.

269
16:44.234 --> 16:45.401
My misery.

270
16:52.158 --> 16:54.786
[birds chirping]

271
16:57.956 --> 16:59.499
Why did you bring me to this house?

272
17:01.000 --> 17:02.293
Little pity, that's all.

273
17:04.212 --> 17:06.840
I figured pity is my best shot at winning you over.

274
17:08.216 --> 17:10.885
So for this month, I'm gonna try everything.

275
17:13.221 --> 17:14.222
What do you say?

276
17:15.348 --> 17:17.600
So does looking at me make your heart ache?

277
17:20.061 --> 17:21.354
What are you thinking?

278
17:23.064 --> 17:24.315
It's not enough, is it?

279
17:26.359 --> 17:27.694
Why aren't you asking…

280
17:28.444 --> 17:31.614
the reason why I suggested we date?

281
17:33.867 --> 17:36.536
-So you feel guilty. -[sentimental Korean pop song playing]

282
17:36.661 --> 17:39.622
I only know two ways to win someone's heart.

283
17:40.081 --> 17:41.583
Making them feel guilty…

284
17:43.418 --> 17:44.419
or just hurting.

285
17:44.544 --> 17:47.255
[vocalist singing in Korean]

286
17:48.923 --> 17:50.383
[sighs deeply]

287
17:51.885 --> 17:53.678
I can get over you in a month.

288
17:57.765 --> 18:01.895
Right now, my feelings for you have definitely peaked.

289
18:02.020 --> 18:04.647
But it's just my feelings getting ahead of themselves.

290
18:05.189 --> 18:08.026
And I'm really selfish, so I never take a loss.

291
18:08.151 --> 18:10.653
I swear, in one month, I'll definitely have moved on.

292
18:10.778 --> 18:12.947
Even if you say you like me, I'll reject you.

293
18:14.490 --> 18:16.034
Can you swear on that?

294
18:19.579 --> 18:21.915
Answer me. Can you swear?

295
18:27.545 --> 18:29.589
I'll do it if you do me one favor.

296
18:30.882 --> 18:32.133
I'm listening.

297
18:37.347 --> 18:40.475
After our dates, for ten seconds, keep eye contact.

298
18:42.352 --> 18:44.729
Ten seconds without breaking means I'm over you.

299
18:52.695 --> 18:53.863
Let's do it now.

300
18:53.988 --> 18:57.867
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

301
18:59.953 --> 19:01.746
[music rises]

302
19:07.961 --> 19:09.545
Wow, so you like me this much?

303
19:11.381 --> 19:13.299
Deok-sun, what you gonna do?

304
19:21.349 --> 19:22.892
I'll last four seconds tomorrow.

305
19:37.740 --> 19:39.993
YEONHWARU

306
19:40.159 --> 19:43.788
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

307
20:14.861 --> 20:16.988
[music softens]

308
20:25.580 --> 20:27.123
[song concludes]

309
20:30.293 --> 20:32.378
[sighs] Come on.

310
20:32.503 --> 20:33.963
Is this really counseling?

311
20:34.088 --> 20:35.214
Of course.

312
20:35.882 --> 20:37.091
If she says so.

313
20:37.884 --> 20:40.803
Is it a good plan you guys hang out together while being divorced?

314
20:40.928 --> 20:42.972
-Of course. -If she says so.

315
20:43.890 --> 20:45.099
[sighs]

316
20:47.477 --> 20:50.146
Mom, Dad, let me change my name.

317
20:51.064 --> 20:53.232
My name is too old-school.

318
20:53.357 --> 20:54.609
I don't like it at all.

319
20:54.734 --> 20:56.152
[both] Forget it!

320
20:59.113 --> 21:00.073
[sighs]

321
21:03.868 --> 21:04.911
[sighs]

322
21:05.036 --> 21:07.580
Is he okay in there or did he fall into the toilet?

323
21:07.705 --> 21:08.998
Why so slow?

324
21:09.999 --> 21:12.335
Let me try to talk him out of it, all right?

325
21:12.460 --> 21:15.213
Name changes are such a hassle with banks and all.

326
21:19.467 --> 21:21.135
Should we just tell him the whole truth?

327
21:23.137 --> 21:24.138
About our divorce?

328
21:26.265 --> 21:27.683
Why we really separated?

329
21:33.397 --> 21:34.482
So back then…

330
21:36.859 --> 21:38.194
I loved you despite it all.

331
21:39.570 --> 21:40.947
Yeah, I asked for a divorce.

332
21:42.448 --> 21:44.283
But you didn't fight for us.

333
21:45.785 --> 21:46.786
[sighs]

334
21:47.954 --> 21:48.913
Hey, Mun-yeong,

335
21:49.747 --> 21:53.042
all I remember is crying and begging you not to leave me.

336
21:54.210 --> 21:55.419
Why are you saying that?

337
21:55.920 --> 21:56.963
That's not it.

338
21:57.880 --> 21:58.965
You let me go.

339
21:59.674 --> 22:03.344
And back then, I really loved you.

340
22:07.390 --> 22:08.391
[Sang-su retches]

341
22:10.476 --> 22:12.895
-[playful guitar music playing] -[groans]

342
22:13.020 --> 22:16.357
I… [groans] I'm taking the bus.

343
22:17.316 --> 22:18.651
I hope you understand.

344
22:19.193 --> 22:20.444
[groans]

345
22:21.195 --> 22:23.197
Hey, Sang-su. Sang-su!

346
22:26.868 --> 22:27.952
[clears throat]

347
22:34.167 --> 22:35.376
First, you gotta dry it.

348
22:35.501 --> 22:36.878
Moisture will make it short-circuit.

349
22:37.503 --> 22:38.546
-Thank you so much. -Thank you.

350
22:43.176 --> 22:45.887
Hey, shouldn't we give him a reward?

351
22:46.012 --> 22:47.972
Mm-mm. He volunteers his expertise.

352
22:48.097 --> 22:49.932
-He used to be a pro. -[man] Really?

353
22:55.813 --> 22:57.064
[music concludes]

354
22:57.190 --> 22:59.692
[Wan-do] Your third chemo is tomorrow. Where are you going?

355
22:59.817 --> 23:00.776
YEAR 2021

356
23:00.902 --> 23:02.445
It spread to my peritoneum.

357
23:02.904 --> 23:04.739
And Opdivo isn't helping.

358
23:05.531 --> 23:06.490
No.

359
23:06.991 --> 23:09.243
There's got to be something else. Another way.

360
23:09.827 --> 23:12.580
My mom, my dad, and even my doctor…

361
23:14.207 --> 23:15.541
they've all given up.

362
23:18.920 --> 23:20.713
Now you just have to give up too.

363
23:27.470 --> 23:30.223
[sobbing]

364
23:38.606 --> 23:42.568
If you just leave like this and go die,

365
23:42.693 --> 23:44.111
I'll live recklessly.

366
23:45.780 --> 23:47.031
I'll ruin my whole life.

367
23:47.698 --> 23:51.160
I'll quit diving forever and drink my life away.

368
23:51.786 --> 23:53.746
I'll let myself become a total mess.

369
23:55.122 --> 23:56.415
I'm even willing to…

370
23:58.668 --> 24:01.337
live a more pathetic life than my sister's.

371
24:02.338 --> 24:04.423
I'm not lying. I mean every word.

372
24:06.133 --> 24:10.596
So if you want to see me ruin my life, then drop dead.

373
24:13.516 --> 24:18.813
-[sobs, sniffles] -[tender guitar music playing]

374
24:19.939 --> 24:21.482
[sobbing]

375
24:27.571 --> 24:28.572
Oh.

376
24:41.502 --> 24:45.423
[light melody playing over music box]

377
24:48.592 --> 24:49.635
[sighs]

378
24:51.804 --> 24:52.930
Can I have it?

379
24:53.431 --> 24:55.891
No, I can't fall asleep without it. You know that.

380
24:56.934 --> 24:57.893
Bo-ra…

381
24:59.020 --> 25:01.522
from now on, I won't leave your side.

382
25:02.481 --> 25:04.650
Until you fall asleep, I'll hold this next to you.

383
25:05.818 --> 25:09.071
The thing is, I'm taking it the second you're out.

384
25:10.614 --> 25:16.203
Since you can't sleep without it, you won't leave without this, right?

385
25:18.080 --> 25:19.081
[exhales softly]

386
25:20.875 --> 25:22.251
I'm really sorry, Wan-do.

387
25:25.838 --> 25:29.842
And I'm really thankful for you not giving up.

388
25:36.640 --> 25:37.600
[exhales sharply]

389
25:38.351 --> 25:39.352
[door opens]

390
25:41.812 --> 25:43.731
-[door closes] -[Namgung groans softly]

391
25:46.609 --> 25:47.818
[grunts softly]

392
25:47.943 --> 25:49.820
[music concludes]

393
25:49.945 --> 25:51.405
How deep is it today?

394
25:51.822 --> 25:53.532
[Wan-do] A hundred-fifty meters.

395
25:54.575 --> 25:55.618
I have news.

396
25:56.243 --> 25:58.788
That music box isn't there.

397
25:59.538 --> 26:00.498
So Bo-ra lied.

398
26:02.625 --> 26:03.667
Of course it is.

399
26:04.960 --> 26:06.337
I just can't find it.

400
26:06.462 --> 26:07.671
[sighs]

401
26:09.048 --> 26:10.174
[inhales deeply]

402
26:13.803 --> 26:14.762
Bro…

403
26:16.389 --> 26:19.475
what if Bo-ra's awake…

404
26:21.185 --> 26:23.312
and can't sleep up there either because of that?

405
26:26.899 --> 26:29.402
It's heaven, I'm pretty sure they have a cure.

406
26:32.488 --> 26:34.365
Hell might not have any, though.

407
26:35.866 --> 26:39.620
-[breathes deeply] -[low somber music playing]

408
26:39.745 --> 26:40.871
It's been three days.

409
26:41.831 --> 26:43.374
I'll give you five days max.

410
26:44.291 --> 26:45.376
And that's it, no more.

411
26:46.460 --> 26:48.295
Eat even if you don't want to.

412
26:48.421 --> 26:51.257
Go to karaoke and sing even if you don't want to.

413
26:52.675 --> 26:54.009
Force yourself to smile.

414
26:54.135 --> 26:55.428
Don't worry those you love.

415
26:56.095 --> 26:59.849
If you force yourself enough, you'll get used to it.

416
27:02.518 --> 27:04.061
You'll survive somehow.

417
27:10.443 --> 27:11.694
Did you do that too?

418
27:12.695 --> 27:13.779
Did that…

419
27:16.240 --> 27:17.450
make life go on?

420
27:18.409 --> 27:21.078
[inhales, sighs heavily]

421
27:21.203 --> 27:22.788
[music concludes]

422
27:24.582 --> 27:26.750
[social worker] So, did Sol call you again?

423
27:28.919 --> 27:29.879
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

424
27:30.004 --> 27:32.131
[social worker] You should know, since the new semester started,

425
27:32.256 --> 27:34.633
I think he's struggling more emotionally.

426
27:34.758 --> 27:37.386
His mother's arrest must have been a tremendous shock for him,

427
27:37.970 --> 27:40.055
and he had to transfer schools suddenly.

428
27:40.723 --> 27:43.350
Is my foster application on hold again?

429
27:43.809 --> 27:45.978
I've completed my community service

430
27:46.103 --> 27:48.647
and finished the whole foster parent training.

431
27:48.772 --> 27:50.232
Are there more documents I need?

432
27:50.357 --> 27:52.651
Well, I'm afraid you're single

433
27:52.776 --> 27:54.820
and with no extra hands around to help you…

434
27:54.945 --> 27:57.198
[inhales deeply, sighs]

435
27:57.323 --> 28:00.951
Things would go more smoothly if Sol's brother applied alongside you.

436
28:01.744 --> 28:03.287
Have you not told him about this yet?

437
28:06.832 --> 28:08.250
I contacted Pastor Kim,

438
28:08.375 --> 28:11.378
and he promised to come back as quickly as he could.

439
28:11.504 --> 28:14.965
Until then, we have someone who's worked in foster care, so we--

440
28:17.760 --> 28:18.844
[sighs]

441
28:25.184 --> 28:26.310
[sighs]

442
28:26.435 --> 28:28.187
[footsteps receding]

443
28:29.063 --> 28:30.397
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

444
28:31.023 --> 28:32.066
[sighs]

445
28:36.820 --> 28:38.739
I first saw him three years ago.

446
28:39.698 --> 28:41.700
After that, he'd call once a month,

447
28:41.825 --> 28:43.702
and I'd make sure he had something to eat.

448
28:44.787 --> 28:47.581
When your mother was arrested, he went to the shelter.

449
28:47.706 --> 28:50.000
He struggled to adjust, so he called often.

450
28:50.543 --> 28:52.169
It's true I didn't tell you.

451
28:52.670 --> 28:55.172
I tried to handle the situation alone.

452
28:55.297 --> 28:58.050
I couldn't hold him back, and I'm truly sorry about that.

453
28:58.175 --> 29:00.052
Do you have any idea why he's in contact?

454
29:01.512 --> 29:03.180
It's for Choi Hwa-young's petition.

455
29:03.722 --> 29:05.224
The trial is set for next week.

456
29:05.349 --> 29:07.935
Namgung, Sol is ten years old.

457
29:08.602 --> 29:11.021
It's for the petition, yes, but he missed you too.

458
29:11.146 --> 29:12.648
He's not a normal kid.

459
29:14.733 --> 29:16.110
I know better than anyone.

460
29:17.570 --> 29:18.904
I was like that at his age.

461
29:20.281 --> 29:22.449
[pensive piano music playing]

462
29:23.117 --> 29:25.828
[sighs] I won't repeat this.

463
29:27.037 --> 29:28.289
Stay out of this.

464
29:29.540 --> 29:30.499
Sorry, I won't.

465
29:36.714 --> 29:37.756
Hey, Mi-do.

466
29:39.008 --> 29:40.593
We ended things between us.

467
29:41.802 --> 29:42.928
Have you forgotten?

468
29:43.470 --> 29:44.722
We're not a couple.

469
29:45.764 --> 29:48.183
You have no right to interfere. Understood?

470
29:48.767 --> 29:50.561
I know. The thing is…

471
29:53.814 --> 29:56.734
what we had went beyond me just being your girlfriend.

472
29:59.236 --> 30:02.448
You help Yeong-do and Wan-do, so I want to do this too.

473
30:02.573 --> 30:03.949
The situation is different.

474
30:05.576 --> 30:07.995
Do you want me to say the reason out loud?

475
30:10.414 --> 30:11.749
I'm telling you clearly.

476
30:13.959 --> 30:15.753
No more interference.

477
30:15.878 --> 30:17.421
I won't go so easy next time.

478
30:17.546 --> 30:22.468
[pensive piano music continues]

479
30:39.026 --> 30:40.027
[scoffs]

480
30:40.819 --> 30:42.029
[sighs]

481
30:46.533 --> 30:47.618
[music concludes]

482
30:48.369 --> 30:49.953
How are you? My name is Sol.

483
30:50.579 --> 30:52.414
Hey, who's that mini-Namgung?

484
30:52.998 --> 30:54.291
He said his name is Sol.

485
30:54.416 --> 30:57.252
It's Sol, like do-re-mi-fa-sol-la-ti-do

486
30:57.378 --> 30:58.545
I'm Han Sol. Hi!

487
31:00.881 --> 31:05.302
[quietly] "All I remember is crying and begging you not to leave me."

488
31:07.846 --> 31:09.515
Heck yeah! [chuckles]

489
31:09.640 --> 31:12.935
The pastor who had agreed to take him in had an emergency.

490
31:13.060 --> 31:14.561
He'll stay with us for a few days.

491
31:16.105 --> 31:18.148
Listen, let's all get along.

492
31:18.565 --> 31:22.027
-Okay! -[chimes tinkling]

493
31:22.152 --> 31:23.529
Auntie!

494
31:28.075 --> 31:29.159
[sighs]

495
31:32.079 --> 31:35.374
Auntie, you told me to call you if I was having a hard time.

496
31:36.125 --> 31:37.960
And living there was really hard.

497
31:41.672 --> 31:45.884
Also, I ended the book you bought me last time, Auntie.

498
31:49.805 --> 31:52.015
So, pretty Mi-do…

499
31:53.267 --> 31:56.395
is Assistant Manager Namgung really angry?

500
31:59.648 --> 32:01.942
Don't call him that. He's your brother.

501
32:02.067 --> 32:05.070
I'll mention him in the petition, but don't expect much.

502
32:05.195 --> 32:07.156
You're prettier than a K-pop star.

503
32:08.115 --> 32:09.283
Still no.

504
32:09.867 --> 32:11.410
You saw your brother's face.

505
32:12.035 --> 32:13.787
He's really scary when he's angry.

506
32:13.912 --> 32:16.707
That's why he put my mom into jail?

507
32:16.832 --> 32:17.875
'Cause he's angry?

508
32:21.295 --> 32:24.214
-[tender guitar music playing] -[sighs]

509
32:32.514 --> 32:33.557
[grunts softly]

510
32:38.854 --> 32:40.189
Han Sol…

511
32:41.690 --> 32:44.610
you think you love your mom more than anyone, don't you?

512
32:46.236 --> 32:47.321
But you're wrong.

513
32:48.280 --> 32:51.241
You've only known your mother for ten years or so,

514
32:52.117 --> 32:54.369
but your brother has known her for 36.

515
32:56.455 --> 32:59.416
She did something wrong, so she ended up in prison

516
32:59.541 --> 33:01.543
as punishment for the wrong she had done.

517
33:02.211 --> 33:03.337
It wasn't his fault.

518
33:10.636 --> 33:11.762
Han Sol…

519
33:13.764 --> 33:15.849
whatever someone else says,

520
33:17.476 --> 33:19.937
hating your brother should never be an option.

521
33:25.734 --> 33:28.320
Promise the girl prettier than a K-pop star.

522
33:29.613 --> 33:30.572
Hmm?

523
33:34.159 --> 33:35.118
You won't?

524
33:38.664 --> 33:39.623
Good job.

525
33:40.999 --> 33:44.086
Jeez. [sighs]

526
33:45.838 --> 33:47.422
Sleep tight. [chuckles softly]

527
34:00.269 --> 34:04.022
REQUESTING A DRIVER UP TO THREE MINUTES AWAY

528
34:04.606 --> 34:06.275
Everyone gone crazy this Friday?

529
34:06.400 --> 34:08.485
-This is Seoul. Why no taxis? -[music concludes]

530
34:08.610 --> 34:11.280
Why would they come? It's a stone's throw away.

531
34:13.198 --> 34:15.450
You should go back. Sol is at home.

532
34:16.952 --> 34:18.954
I only came out to breathe for a minute.

533
34:19.955 --> 34:20.998
[scoffs]

534
34:23.250 --> 34:25.127
[chuckles]

535
34:26.128 --> 34:27.963
-[laughs] -What?

536
34:28.088 --> 34:29.298
Why are you laughing?

537
34:29.923 --> 34:31.383
Don't you think it's funny?

538
34:31.508 --> 34:33.051
That child is calling you "Auntie."

539
34:33.176 --> 34:34.428
[gasps]

540
34:34.553 --> 34:36.054
He does it on purpose.

541
34:36.179 --> 34:38.015
He knows I hate being called that.

542
34:38.682 --> 34:41.852
Mi-do, you're old enough

543
34:41.977 --> 34:43.770
-to be called "Auntie" now… -[gasps]

544
34:43.896 --> 34:46.315
-…so he's right. -[Mi-do gasps]

545
34:46.440 --> 34:48.483
You are an auntie, a total auntie.

546
34:48.609 --> 34:49.610
Oh, come on!

547
34:50.152 --> 34:54.114
-What are you even saying? -[laughs]

548
34:55.949 --> 34:57.743
Obvious he and Hoya are brothers.

549
35:01.663 --> 35:02.915
He doesn't look like him.

550
35:03.040 --> 35:07.169
Come to think of it, the first time I met Hoya,

551
35:07.294 --> 35:08.837
I was exactly your age.

552
35:11.214 --> 35:12.215
[chuckles]

553
35:15.344 --> 35:16.386
Your socks.

554
35:17.012 --> 35:17.971
Huh?

555
35:18.430 --> 35:19.473
Goodness.

556
35:21.308 --> 35:22.976
Jeez. [groans]

557
35:25.354 --> 35:28.815
Know why you always catch a cold around this time?

558
35:28.941 --> 35:29.983
This is why.

559
35:30.108 --> 35:31.109
Because you're so careless.

560
35:31.234 --> 35:33.195
-[soft emotional music playing] -Hey, Mom, stop. What are you doing?

561
35:33.320 --> 35:35.781
Oh, just stay still, okay?

562
35:36.406 --> 35:37.866
The bus won't be here for a while.

563
35:37.991 --> 35:39.743
No, Mom, you wear it.

564
35:39.868 --> 35:42.204
You're the one with asthma this time of year.

565
35:42.996 --> 35:44.081
Jeez.

566
35:56.635 --> 35:58.053
This is all your fault.

567
36:00.097 --> 36:02.975
When you were a child, if you were even a little hurt,

568
36:03.100 --> 36:05.978
you'd run to me and say, "It hurts here, Mommy."

569
36:06.103 --> 36:09.064
You'd act like you were dying and beg for a doctor.

570
36:09.898 --> 36:12.651
Now that you're an adult, you don't even say a word.

571
36:12.776 --> 36:13.860
Am I wrong?

572
36:15.070 --> 36:16.279
So how would I know?

573
36:17.906 --> 36:19.783
I thought you were dressed warmly.

574
36:21.118 --> 36:23.745
I never thought the wind would get in through there.

575
36:24.496 --> 36:25.914
[music rises]

576
36:28.500 --> 36:31.795
[Mi-do sobbing]

577
36:34.172 --> 36:37.426
If you act like this, what does that make me?

578
36:38.218 --> 36:41.930
I was going to be the one to apologize first. [sobs]

579
36:43.348 --> 36:45.642
I never apologized to you.

580
36:46.101 --> 36:47.352
I was only blaming you.

581
36:48.854 --> 36:51.815
[sobs] Then I won't apologize either, I won't.

582
36:51.940 --> 36:53.316
I don't want to, all right?

583
36:54.484 --> 36:58.196
I'm so embarrassed right now, I feel like I'm gonna die.

584
36:59.322 --> 37:03.285
[sobs] I'm being treated like garbage every single day.

585
37:03.869 --> 37:06.538
Those Gen Zs treat me like absolute trash.

586
37:08.165 --> 37:10.167
I'm so humiliated, I could die.

587
37:10.709 --> 37:13.003
So why are you being like this right now?

588
37:13.128 --> 37:15.922
And so, that's why it's just…

589
37:16.506 --> 37:18.383
Go ahead, let it all out.

590
37:19.301 --> 37:22.220
Please, go ahead and blame your mom to survive out there.

591
37:23.430 --> 37:25.265
Oh, my. [laughs]

592
37:25.390 --> 37:27.184
Look at you, still a baby.

593
37:28.268 --> 37:30.062
Not an auntie. Baby.

594
37:30.812 --> 37:34.232
I'm only crying because of everything you're doing, that's why.

595
37:34.483 --> 37:40.864
[sobbing]

596
37:46.411 --> 37:48.121
[music concludes]

597
37:48.246 --> 37:49.581
[door opens]

598
37:51.124 --> 37:52.209
Thank you.

599
37:56.546 --> 37:57.798
Hi, son.

600
38:00.634 --> 38:03.678
Time's not on our side, so let me cut right to it.

601
38:05.222 --> 38:07.015
You're here about Sol's custody, right?

602
38:09.684 --> 38:11.311
Commissary money won't cut it.

603
38:12.062 --> 38:14.356
Leniency petitions, that's not enough.

604
38:15.982 --> 38:19.152
I want the best lawyer you can find to get me out of here.

605
38:19.277 --> 38:20.779
Get me the best lawyer.

606
38:22.989 --> 38:25.784
By the way, Mi-do came to see me more than once.

607
38:26.493 --> 38:29.830
If you refuse to help me, Mi-do will know about it.

608
38:34.000 --> 38:35.418
Sure. Understood.

609
38:38.338 --> 38:39.339
Come on.

610
38:39.965 --> 38:40.924
Just like that?

611
38:41.341 --> 38:44.261
There are four questions I need to ask you before I say yes.

612
38:46.638 --> 38:51.434
If you get even one of them right, I'll accept all your terms.

613
38:53.895 --> 38:54.855
Okay.

614
38:56.314 --> 38:57.399
First one.

615
38:58.900 --> 39:00.277
What's Sol's shoe size?

616
39:03.113 --> 39:04.197
[sighs]

617
39:04.781 --> 39:06.241
[chuckles derisively]

618
39:06.783 --> 39:07.951
[sighs]

619
39:09.661 --> 39:11.580
180-- 170 millimeters.

620
39:12.581 --> 39:14.249
I'm not sure. Kids grow fast.

621
39:14.374 --> 39:18.170
Second, the name of Sol's school.

622
39:19.087 --> 39:22.549
[scoffs] He's been transferred so many times.

623
39:23.717 --> 39:25.760
I know his old one for sure. I can tell it to you.

624
39:25.886 --> 39:26.845
Third…

625
39:28.221 --> 39:30.223
Sol's best friend's name.

626
39:30.974 --> 39:31.933
[scoffs]

627
39:32.434 --> 39:35.645
Fourth, Sol's birthday.

628
39:37.147 --> 39:38.231
[scoffs]

629
39:41.651 --> 39:42.652
[sighs]

630
39:43.737 --> 39:45.697
I thought you'd get at least one right.

631
39:48.200 --> 39:49.242
I'm disappointed.

632
39:50.368 --> 39:51.620
[inhales deeply]

633
39:52.579 --> 39:55.665
Today you'll be receiving a document about parental rights.

634
40:06.259 --> 40:08.053
[heavy equipment case thuds]

635
40:08.178 --> 40:11.598
[Mi-do grunting]

636
40:12.641 --> 40:13.850
[sighs] Jeez.

637
40:17.604 --> 40:18.980
[sighs]

638
40:19.105 --> 40:21.107
[breathes deeply]

639
40:21.983 --> 40:23.777
[team leader] Here they are, meet my team.

640
40:26.196 --> 40:27.822
This is the new lawyer working with us,

641
40:28.323 --> 40:30.450
Han Tae-seung. Such a pleasure.

642
40:30.992 --> 40:33.662
[laughs] He's seriously good-looking, right?

643
40:34.162 --> 40:36.665
We'll hit 100K now. [laughs]

644
40:39.251 --> 40:40.168
Oh?

645
40:42.963 --> 40:45.590
Are you… Director Lee Mi-do?

646
40:45.715 --> 40:48.343
-[quirky upbeat music playing] -[Tae-seung] You are, right?

647
40:48.760 --> 40:52.555
She directed that great movie. The 13th Season.

648
40:53.181 --> 40:56.142
Wow. I saw it like a million times.

649
40:56.601 --> 40:57.560
This is amazing.

650
40:58.311 --> 40:59.729
Should we start setting the lighting?

651
41:00.522 --> 41:04.526
Uh, yeah. Let's prepare everything. Get ready. Let's do this today, huh?

652
41:06.111 --> 41:07.153
[quietly] You got this.

653
41:07.696 --> 41:09.114
[exhales]

654
41:11.950 --> 41:12.909
Hey, Ms. Lee.

655
41:13.493 --> 41:15.954
-Hmm? -You can't plug it in like this.

656
41:16.705 --> 41:17.664
I'm sorry.

657
41:18.873 --> 41:20.834
[team member 1] Move to the right a bit.

658
41:20.959 --> 41:22.168
No, left, left.

659
41:22.294 --> 41:24.462
A bit more. Down, down a bit.

660
41:24.587 --> 41:26.965
[sighs] You really have no clue, do you?

661
41:27.090 --> 41:28.466
I'm really sorry.

662
41:28.591 --> 41:31.052
Hey, Ms. Lee, I told you to leave enough headroom.

663
41:31.177 --> 41:32.721
Yes, I'm truly sorry.

664
41:34.347 --> 41:35.515
[team member 2] Ms. Lee?

665
41:35.640 --> 41:36.683
-Yes? -[team member 1] Ms. Lee.

666
41:36.808 --> 41:38.476
-Yes? -[team member 2] Ms. Lee?

667
41:38.601 --> 41:39.644
Yes?

668
41:44.024 --> 41:45.066
[sighs]

669
41:46.860 --> 41:47.986
[sighs heavily]

670
41:49.612 --> 41:50.655
[sighs]

671
41:50.780 --> 41:52.741
-[music concludes] -[exhales sharply]

672
41:54.075 --> 41:55.744
I'm telling you this as a friend.

673
41:55.869 --> 41:57.412
[classical music playing over speakers]

674
41:57.537 --> 42:00.165
Your aesthetic only worked because they were films.

675
42:00.790 --> 42:02.792
-Editing isn't easy. -[cell phone vibrating]

676
42:02.917 --> 42:04.294
TIN CAN BASTARD

677
42:07.505 --> 42:08.923
[Yeon-ju] Do a movie adaptation.

678
42:09.049 --> 42:13.136
So, there's a story about a girl who cheats on her long-term partner.

679
42:13.261 --> 42:16.056
The whole thing starts with the boyfriend trying to kill her.

680
42:16.181 --> 42:18.808
[coughs]

681
42:22.771 --> 42:24.898
And then? Does he?

682
42:25.023 --> 42:26.608
Here's where it gets good.

683
42:26.733 --> 42:28.276
You know the guy who hit on her?

684
42:28.401 --> 42:30.862
Turns out he's also trying to murder her.

685
42:31.821 --> 42:32.864
Why does he…

686
42:33.323 --> 42:36.242
It turns out the boyfriend and the guy she cheated with

687
42:36.368 --> 42:37.994
were the real couple the whole time.

688
42:38.119 --> 42:39.454
[gasps]

689
42:39.579 --> 42:42.457
So the one who ends up killing her isn't the boyfriend.

690
42:43.166 --> 42:44.167
[door bell tinkles]

691
42:44.751 --> 42:46.169
Oh, hi, Attorney Han.

692
42:46.628 --> 42:48.046
-Over here. -[gasps softly]

693
42:52.217 --> 42:54.135
Director Lee. [chuckles]

694
42:54.260 --> 42:55.553
It's been a while.

695
42:58.765 --> 42:59.891
Hmm. Right.

696
43:01.101 --> 43:03.353
-Doing good these days? -Uh…

697
43:03.478 --> 43:04.604
Have a seat here.

698
43:04.729 --> 43:05.980
[cell phone vibrates]

699
43:08.274 --> 43:09.526
[Tae-seung sighs]

700
43:09.651 --> 43:11.653
[Yeon-ju] Hey, I think he's interested in me.

701
43:11.778 --> 43:15.031
He kept asking where I was, so I had no choice.

702
43:15.657 --> 43:17.492
Take the hint and leave early.

703
43:19.160 --> 43:22.497
-[chuckles, sighs] -[soft playful music playing]

704
43:23.498 --> 43:25.542
[Tae-seung] Thank you, sir. Get her home safely.

705
43:32.507 --> 43:34.008
You didn't answer my calls, so I had to.

706
43:35.301 --> 43:38.888
For someone who had no choice, you sure had fun with Yeon-ju.

707
43:41.599 --> 43:42.851
Are you jealous?

708
43:47.272 --> 43:48.731
Are you going to kill me?

709
43:48.857 --> 43:50.483
Where did that come out of?

710
43:50.608 --> 43:51.776
[scoffs]

711
43:53.862 --> 43:56.197
I'm sorry for not answering your calls.

712
43:57.740 --> 44:01.119
Thirty-six years old, and I'm being talked down to

713
44:01.244 --> 44:03.872
by kids half my age while barely scraping by.

714
44:03.997 --> 44:06.207
[inhales deeply] I hated it.

715
44:07.375 --> 44:08.751
It felt so pathetic.

716
44:10.086 --> 44:12.922
I just couldn't bring myself to answer your phone calls.

717
44:17.469 --> 44:21.014
I told you to get back up if you feel embarrassed. Funny, right?

718
44:23.141 --> 44:24.100
Yeah.

719
44:29.439 --> 44:31.024
Serves you right. Mm.

720
44:31.524 --> 44:32.650
Jeez.

721
44:34.486 --> 44:35.445
[chuckles]

722
44:36.696 --> 44:37.864
I'll treat you to dinner.

723
44:38.865 --> 44:40.408
You deserve something good to eat.

724
44:45.580 --> 44:46.623
[chuckles softly]

725
44:49.042 --> 44:50.543
I thought it was cute.

726
44:51.586 --> 44:53.421
A woman who looks like she's in her twenties,

727
44:53.546 --> 44:56.174
scraping by and trying so hard to survive.

728
44:57.592 --> 44:58.968
Aw, so cute.

729
45:01.596 --> 45:02.597
[chuckles softly]

730
45:07.018 --> 45:08.728
[music concludes]

731
45:08.853 --> 45:12.649
-[indistinct chatter] -[soft music playing over speakers]

732
45:13.191 --> 45:14.859
That wasn't my first hotel.

733
45:16.736 --> 45:18.029
I just panicked a little.

734
45:18.154 --> 45:19.656
I have been to hotels with guys.

735
45:20.698 --> 45:21.866
Really?

736
45:22.784 --> 45:23.743
How many?

737
45:26.579 --> 45:29.165
Like, uh, five or six?

738
45:29.666 --> 45:30.875
Hmm!

739
45:32.585 --> 45:33.878
No, wait a sec.

740
45:34.003 --> 45:36.339
Sun-cheol left, his mom called halfway through.

741
45:37.423 --> 45:39.217
So then, maybe two.

742
45:39.717 --> 45:40.802
Hey.

743
45:41.469 --> 45:42.762
What about you?

744
45:42.887 --> 45:44.305
How many women have you been with?

745
45:46.182 --> 45:48.059
Babe, I only have eyes for you.

746
45:48.768 --> 45:50.853
Honey, you're my one and only love.

747
45:52.355 --> 45:55.066
Sweetheart, that's what you say when your boyfriend asks.

748
45:55.191 --> 45:56.651
Don't say two or three guys.

749
45:58.194 --> 45:59.195
Silly.

750
46:04.993 --> 46:05.994
Eye contact now.

751
46:06.578 --> 46:07.537
We haven't done it today.

752
46:07.954 --> 46:09.289
Can't even last four seconds.

753
46:09.414 --> 46:10.373
So?

754
46:10.915 --> 46:12.250
It was an oath we swore.

755
46:14.711 --> 46:15.670
[sighs]

756
46:19.257 --> 46:20.300
Whenever you're ready.

757
46:20.425 --> 46:22.302
[breathes deeply]

758
46:23.761 --> 46:24.846
Okay, I'm ready.

759
46:27.348 --> 46:31.477
[playful piano music playing]

760
46:33.855 --> 46:34.814
[gasps softly]

761
46:35.773 --> 46:37.317
-[Namgung] Jeez, look at you. -[sighs]

762
46:37.442 --> 46:38.568
Why keep doing this?

763
46:39.527 --> 46:41.029
It's too much pressure, huh?

764
46:41.154 --> 46:42.739
Can't even hold it for four seconds?

765
46:44.532 --> 46:45.783
Should I stop shaving?

766
46:46.492 --> 46:47.744
What should I do?

767
46:49.495 --> 46:50.622
Let's try again.

768
46:51.289 --> 46:52.999
Something got in my eye, so I closed it.

769
46:53.124 --> 46:54.500
We're done for today.

770
46:54.626 --> 46:55.877
Come on, just one last time.

771
46:59.380 --> 47:00.923
[music concludes]

772
47:10.350 --> 47:11.392
[scoffs]

773
47:16.981 --> 47:19.442
[soft music playing over speakers]

774
47:22.612 --> 47:25.490
[munching loudly]

775
47:28.034 --> 47:29.869
Since it seems fate brought us here,

776
47:31.079 --> 47:34.999
how about we discuss some ground rules for the next month?

777
47:37.585 --> 47:41.214
Uh… like dividing up our regular spots so we don't overlap.

778
47:41.923 --> 47:45.510
Oh, did you two block each other's numbers?

779
47:46.260 --> 47:47.303
Don't say you didn't.

780
47:49.013 --> 47:50.348
[softly] Wow.

781
47:51.474 --> 47:53.309
Even for a month, that's just standard etiquette.

782
47:54.686 --> 47:55.728
Don't you agree?

783
47:57.397 --> 47:58.856
I want one of you to move out.

784
47:59.565 --> 48:02.652
I don't care which one of you does it, but get it done immediately.

785
48:02.777 --> 48:04.153
Living right across the hall?

786
48:05.029 --> 48:06.239
I won't accept it.

787
48:07.365 --> 48:08.950
-Isn't that right? -[inhales sharply]

788
48:10.201 --> 48:11.619
Shall we get going?

789
48:12.662 --> 48:13.621
[Tae-seung] Why?

790
48:14.455 --> 48:15.998
They haven't brought our food yet.

791
48:21.838 --> 48:22.797
Oh.

792
48:31.180 --> 48:32.223
[scoffs]

793
48:33.141 --> 48:34.308
Oh, my.

794
48:34.434 --> 48:36.602
MI-DO, NAMGUNG

795
48:36.811 --> 48:41.065
[poignant instrumental music playing]

796
48:42.734 --> 48:43.693
[gasps softly]

797
48:52.243 --> 48:53.494
I'll be taking this.

798
48:54.078 --> 48:55.163
Level three.

799
48:56.414 --> 48:58.332
Mi-do's rage meter is at level three.

800
49:01.169 --> 49:02.211
[exhales]

801
49:03.379 --> 49:04.547
Level four.

802
49:06.716 --> 49:08.009
Wanna see level five?

803
49:11.888 --> 49:14.515
Keep your boyfriend from acting cocky.

804
49:17.810 --> 49:18.770
Let's go.

805
49:20.730 --> 49:22.106
Hey, wait.

806
49:22.231 --> 49:23.858
Whose fault do you think this is?

807
49:24.609 --> 49:25.568
[exhales sharply]

808
49:28.988 --> 49:30.031
[sighs]

809
49:38.748 --> 49:40.041
It's your fault, of course.

810
49:41.667 --> 49:43.920
You're being so damn clueless, so it's on you.

811
49:46.380 --> 49:48.591
Given their history, show some manners.

812
50:00.812 --> 50:02.980
Let's go, Assistant Manager.

813
50:10.780 --> 50:13.574
[music rises]

814
50:21.916 --> 50:28.339
[breathes deeply]

815
50:32.301 --> 50:33.845
-[music concludes] -[Su-a scoffs]

816
50:34.428 --> 50:35.930
I should have called you "babe."

817
50:36.389 --> 50:38.140
"Assistant Manager," really?

818
50:39.308 --> 50:40.935
Is that really the issue here?

819
50:41.936 --> 50:42.895
What?

820
50:43.396 --> 50:49.527
Is she-- I mean, Ms. Lee, is she getting in your head?

821
50:51.654 --> 50:52.905
Actually, you are.

822
50:54.448 --> 50:56.242
Your face is so red right now.

823
50:56.784 --> 50:58.077
You can let go, you know.

824
51:00.454 --> 51:01.539
[grumbles softly]

825
51:02.874 --> 51:04.250
Just talk about anything else.

826
51:05.459 --> 51:07.295
I know, work. Let's talk about work.

827
51:09.380 --> 51:10.590
Uh…

828
51:11.674 --> 51:13.843
How did Team 3's cost adjustment go?

829
51:13.968 --> 51:15.428
Don't even get me started.

830
51:15.553 --> 51:17.513
I worked late all week because of that.

831
51:18.848 --> 51:19.849
But…

832
51:20.474 --> 51:21.976
Manager Eom pulled it off.

833
51:23.436 --> 51:24.395
Wait, how?

834
51:25.605 --> 51:26.981
As you know, local supply,

835
51:27.106 --> 51:29.692
imported raw material prices vary based on it.

836
51:30.401 --> 51:33.446
He used the increased crop volume as a basis to bluff a bit.

837
51:34.947 --> 51:36.115
That's a relief.

838
51:36.657 --> 51:39.911
If it didn't pass, then that launch would have been hard.

839
51:40.578 --> 51:41.537
Hmm.

840
51:42.413 --> 51:43.623
[exhales]

841
51:43.748 --> 51:47.251
I think I'm calm now, finally. Hmm.

842
52:00.765 --> 52:02.099
[sighs]

843
52:06.312 --> 52:07.480
Whenever someone…

844
52:09.815 --> 52:12.401
asks me what my happiest memory is,

845
52:13.986 --> 52:17.782
I always say it's seeing Lake Lucerne at 22.

846
52:19.951 --> 52:23.120
It was so beautiful, I was speechless just staring at it.

847
52:26.999 --> 52:28.250
But that's a lie.

848
52:31.462 --> 52:33.089
What actually I think of…

849
52:34.840 --> 52:37.593
is incredibly ordinary and unsophisticated.

850
52:39.428 --> 52:42.848
[sentimental piano music playing]

851
52:42.974 --> 52:45.643
When my dad came back from out-of-town training,

852
52:46.852 --> 52:49.355
I stood by the road closest to our house.

853
52:49.855 --> 52:51.065
I was waiting for him.

854
52:53.693 --> 52:55.361
His team bus arrived.

855
52:56.570 --> 53:00.908
He got off, saw me, and carried me home on his back.

856
53:05.538 --> 53:07.957
Strangely, that's my happiest memory.

857
53:10.501 --> 53:12.795
Do you know what my goal for the month is?

858
53:15.464 --> 53:19.802
If anybody asks you what your happiest memory is,

859
53:21.679 --> 53:23.973
you'll probably think of something with Ms. Lee.

860
53:25.099 --> 53:26.142
But I'd like…

861
53:27.768 --> 53:29.020
for just a second…

862
53:31.397 --> 53:33.983
for a memory of us to cross your mind.

863
53:35.776 --> 53:36.861
And it'll happen.

864
53:37.611 --> 53:38.571
I'll…

865
53:40.072 --> 53:41.282
make sure of that.

866
53:53.044 --> 53:54.795
It started back in Haemado.

867
53:57.048 --> 53:59.008
Since Haemado, I'm attracted to you.

868
54:03.387 --> 54:05.097
You're my first love, actually.

869
54:06.015 --> 54:09.268
[music rises]

870
54:14.732 --> 54:16.525
[music concludes]

871
54:16.650 --> 54:18.152
Hey, I did nothing wrong.

872
54:19.236 --> 54:20.946
Anyone else would have done the same.

873
54:22.156 --> 54:24.867
[breathes deeply]

874
54:28.496 --> 54:32.541
When I asked you to date me for a month, I was just using you.

875
54:34.835 --> 54:39.090
The only reason I dated you was so Namgung would date around.

876
54:41.842 --> 54:44.345
I hurt him so much with my actions.

877
54:45.596 --> 54:48.015
I assumed my own suffering would even the score.

878
54:48.766 --> 54:49.767
[gasps softly]

879
54:54.772 --> 54:56.440
You like me for a reason.

880
54:58.275 --> 54:59.443
Namgung and I…

881
55:01.278 --> 55:02.571
we look special.

882
55:04.156 --> 55:05.908
And that's what you want, isn't it?

883
55:07.743 --> 55:08.828
You're right.

884
55:10.788 --> 55:11.872
I want it.

885
55:15.084 --> 55:18.170
I want absolutely everything you gave to Namgung.

886
55:19.046 --> 55:20.131
All of it.

887
55:25.010 --> 55:28.389
[soft instrumental music playing]

888
55:35.396 --> 55:36.814
I have to ask you this.

889
55:40.067 --> 55:44.405
Before, you said if you had to save either Namgung or me,

890
55:44.864 --> 55:47.575
you'd save him without a second thought, right?

891
55:49.076 --> 55:50.077
What if…

892
55:52.371 --> 55:54.206
it was your father instead of me?

893
55:57.668 --> 55:59.170
If you could pick your father…

894
56:02.882 --> 56:05.009
would you still save Namgung?

895
56:16.270 --> 56:17.479
[sighs]

896
56:26.447 --> 56:28.115
[Su-a] It started back in Haemado.

897
56:29.617 --> 56:31.493
Since Haemado, I'm attracted to you.

898
56:32.620 --> 56:34.538
You're my first love, actually.

899
56:37.208 --> 56:38.292
[cell phone vibrates]

900
56:41.587 --> 56:43.797
YEONHUI-DONG TWIN FISTS

901
56:43.923 --> 56:45.257
[Suk-hee] He's such a gentle kid.

902
56:46.008 --> 56:47.676
He's gentler than you, Hoya.

903
56:50.012 --> 56:52.264
DELETE

904
57:07.696 --> 57:09.573
[Namgung] I thought you'd get at least one right.

905
57:10.282 --> 57:11.242
I'm disappointed.

906
57:12.243 --> 57:13.452
Are you really doing this?

907
57:14.119 --> 57:15.204
Son!

908
57:20.626 --> 57:21.835
[inhales sharply]

909
57:21.961 --> 57:23.212
[music concludes]

910
57:28.968 --> 57:30.010
Son.

911
57:41.272 --> 57:44.191
On May 12th, 2025…

912
57:47.152 --> 57:48.320
on Sol's birthday,

913
57:49.738 --> 57:52.533
he took 10,000 won from your wallet without asking,

914
57:53.158 --> 57:56.078
in front of his best friend Eom Ji-eun, remember?

915
57:58.038 --> 58:01.542
You struck him in the face with a shoe three times.

916
58:06.672 --> 58:09.008
Shop owners near Daejun Elementary reported it

917
58:09.133 --> 58:11.135
and child abuse charges were filed.

918
58:11.260 --> 58:14.138
But it ended with a brief statement calling it discipline.

919
58:15.681 --> 58:18.434
You were released without facing consequences.

920
58:21.145 --> 58:23.439
That happened nine times to Han Sol.

921
58:25.691 --> 58:27.609
And for me, the total was 12.

922
58:29.653 --> 58:31.155
Do you have any idea…

923
58:33.824 --> 58:35.451
what I felt the first time…

924
58:37.369 --> 58:39.455
I met the people I love…

925
58:41.165 --> 58:43.667
and am grateful to thanks to you?

926
58:47.171 --> 58:48.464
Deep bitterness.

927
58:50.090 --> 58:51.675
Resentment that I survived.

928
58:51.800 --> 58:53.052
Do you know that?

929
58:57.431 --> 59:01.852
[poignant instrumental music playing]

930
59:06.648 --> 59:07.733
[scoffs]

931
59:13.489 --> 59:14.573
[sighs]

932
59:15.199 --> 59:16.700
[music rises]

933
59:27.252 --> 59:29.588
-[breathes deeply] -[Tae-seung] What if…

934
59:30.672 --> 59:35.177
If you could pick your father, would you still save Namgung?

935
59:38.722 --> 59:42.142
How can you love the man who caused your father's passing?

936
59:42.267 --> 59:46.522
[poignant instrumental music continues]

937
59:48.899 --> 59:54.363
[breathes deeply]

938
01:00:08.961 --> 01:00:10.212
[elevator bell dings]

939
01:00:27.062 --> 01:00:30.315
[Mi-do] Namgung and I first met 29 years ago.

940
01:00:32.443 --> 01:00:35.487
It was an unusually cold winter at the Gangneung coast.

941
01:00:44.955 --> 01:00:47.833
[young Suk-hee sobbing]

942
01:00:53.046 --> 01:00:56.925
[wails loudly]

943
01:01:00.846 --> 01:01:03.098
Oh, my God. Honey, wake up.

944
01:01:03.807 --> 01:01:06.477
Wake up. [sobs]

945
01:01:06.602 --> 01:01:08.562
No!

946
01:01:08.687 --> 01:01:13.525
[screaming]

947
01:01:17.404 --> 01:01:21.783
[Mi-do] The day I met Namgung was the saddest day of my life.

948
01:01:23.160 --> 01:01:26.455
[young Suk-hee wailing] Wake up!

949
01:01:26.580 --> 01:01:27.873
[Mi-do] And that day was the day…

950
01:01:28.916 --> 01:01:31.418
Namgung died for the 12th time.

951
01:01:32.377 --> 01:01:35.839
[young Suk-hee] Honey! [sobs]

952
01:01:37.132 --> 01:01:42.721
[sobbing, wailing]

953
01:02:02.658 --> 01:02:05.911
[music rises]

954
01:02:23.762 --> 01:02:25.639
[music concludes]

955
01:02:25.764 --> 01:02:30.644
[waves crashing gently]

956
01:02:30.769 --> 01:02:34.606
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

957
01:02:34.731 --> 01:02:39.611
["Somewhere in Between" playing]

958
01:02:39.736 --> 01:02:43.156
TAKE GOOD CARE OF HER UNTIL SHE CAN AFFORD TO BUY AN APARTMENT

959
01:02:43.282 --> 01:02:44.616
LEE MI-DO

960
01:02:47.744 --> 01:02:49.371
THANK YOU TO KIM YOON-HYE FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

961
01:02:50.247 --> 01:02:51.832
Oh, your army buddy.

962
01:02:51.957 --> 01:02:54.042
[Tae-seung] Are you trying to fill the void of the father you killed?

963
01:02:54.167 --> 01:02:55.586
Who made Mi-do like that?

964
01:02:55.711 --> 01:02:56.795
It was you.

965
01:02:56.920 --> 01:03:00.465
[Mi-do] Namgung, I just wanted to give you absolutely everything.

966
01:03:00.591 --> 01:03:02.926
[Namgung] The thing you said at the convenience store,

967
01:03:03.051 --> 01:03:05.387
can you repeat it so I can hear it again?

968
01:03:05.512 --> 01:03:07.889
Namgung! I'm not gonna hate you.

969
01:03:08.015 --> 01:03:09.725
-[sobs] -[Mi-do] I can't leave Namgung's side.

970
01:03:10.392 --> 01:03:11.893
He needs me to be there!

971
01:03:16.106 --> 01:03:17.357
[song concludes]
